WEBVTT
NOTE Cedwyn film, frame 006, en. Timings are estimates from the script until the clip is rendered.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.154
<v the Man from the Estate>Bore da. Mind the boxes. You asked about a lease from fifteen forty-seven. A thousand years.

2
00:00:06.504 --> 00:00:14.196
<v Nia>Sir George Herbert to someone called Vaughan, a thousand-year lease of Cydwin. That's how the family research note puts it.

3
00:00:14.546 --> 00:00:16.854
<v the Man from the Estate>And the lease itself? The parchment?

4
00:00:17.204 --> 00:00:26.435
<v Nia>Not held. Nobody on our side has seen the original yet. The evidence catalogue files it as a primary document still to be found.

5
00:00:26.785 --> 00:00:34.477
<v the Man from the Estate>So for now it's a note about a document, not the document. No terms, no boundaries, no signatures to read.

6
00:00:34.827 --> 00:00:42.904
<v Nia>Exactly. And Cydwin is only tied to Great House Farm through the Cedwyn place-name index. A cross-reference, not a proven link.

7
00:00:43.254 --> 00:00:47.869
<v the Man from the Estate>What about the Bute side? Fifteen fifty-two to eighteen twenty-four, you wrote.

8
00:00:48.219 --> 00:00:56.296
<v Nia>Same family research note. It reports Bute estate records naming the holding Cedfin, Cydfin, Ken fin Farm, or Tŷ Mawr Farm.

9
00:00:56.646 --> 00:00:59.723
<v the Man from the Estate>Which records, though? Which box, which reference number?

10
00:01:00.073 --> 00:01:08.150
<v Nia>That's the gap. The documents haven't been produced. No dates, no archive references, nothing tying those names to Great House Farm.

11
00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:16.962
<v Nia>Then there's this. Mary (Nancy) Williams's own statement. She sets down that the Williams family were on the farm from sixteen sixty-seven.

12
00:01:17.312 --> 00:01:20.773
<v the Man from the Estate>Sixteen sixty-seven. Three and a half centuries of Williamses.

13
00:01:21.123 --> 00:01:30.738
<v Nia>That date rests on her statement. The Master Timeline on the Legal Wiki lists it that way, and an earlier written source is still awaited.

14
00:01:31.088 --> 00:01:35.319
<v the Man from the Estate>A family's memory is still a record. It just needs company.

15
00:01:35.669 --> 00:01:41.438
<v Nia>Company, I can offer. The Percy Randell collection. Estate plans, seventeen eighty-six to eighteen thirty-two.

16
00:01:41.788 --> 00:01:43.588
<v the Man from the Estate>Whose estate?

17
00:01:43.938 --> 00:01:51.246
<v Nia>Herbert of White Friars, and the William Hurst estate. Lands in Cogan, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, Penarth, St Andrews Major and Sully.

18
00:01:51.596 --> 00:01:55.827
<v the Man from the Estate>Real maps, then. Field lines you can put your finger on.

19
00:01:56.177 --> 00:02:03.100
<v Nia>Logged in our media register as MR-0223. What they show of our farm, we'll learn field by field.

20
00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:05.250
<v the Man from the Estate>And the thousand-year lease?

21
00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:12.523
<v Nia>Stays on the list marked 'still looking'. Next, the seventeen-ninety plan and the eighteen-hundred survey of Tŷ Mawr.
